  "notes": "Lamb Weston Holdings, Inc. (NYSE: LW). World's #2 frozen-potato processor (frozen french fries / formed potato products) \u2014 supplies QSR (McDonald's, Wendy's, Yum, Chick-fil-A) globally. Spun out of ConAgra Brands Nov 2016. Fiscal year ends last Sunday of May (52/53-week). Data from SEC EDGAR XBRL companyfacts (CIK 0001679273). EBITDA = operating income + D&A. Net debt = LongTermDebt + LongTermDebtAndCapitalLeaseObligationsCurrent \u2212 cash. Major M&A: Feb 2023 acquired remaining 50% of Lamb-Weston/Meijer EMEA JV (~$936M cash + assumed debt ~$430M) \u2014 added FY23 partial-year and full FY24 EMEA consolidation. Prior to FY23 EMEA was equity-method (revenue not consolidated). FY23 net income $1.0B includes ~$401M one-time gain on JV step-up (acquisition-date fair value). FY25 saw normalized post-COVID demand softening + ERP-implementation disruption.",
